course: dictionary
lesson: 839
title: Gentle words for hard times
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words help us talk kindly about sad things. Bereavement is one of them. It means losing a close relative or friend because they have died. It can also mean the sad time that follows. The word is formal, so you will often see it in letters, leaflets and notices.
explain: Use the context to work it out. «Many churches run bereavement support groups; people of all beliefs use counsellors and helplines.» The clues are support groups, counsellors and helplines. These are there to help people who are sad after someone has died. So bereavement must be about that kind of loss.
explain: Notice that the sentence does not say who the people are or what they believe. It says people of all beliefs can use these groups. That is a clue about kindness too: the help is for everyone who is grieving, whatever their religion or background.
fact: Bereavement means the loss of a close relative or friend because they have died.
fact: Bereavement can also mean the sad time and feelings that come after such a loss.
fact: Bereavement is a formal word, so it is often used in letters, leaflets and official notices.
fact: Phrases you may see: «suffer a bereavement», «a family bereavement», «bereavement counselling» and «bereavement leave».
fact: Bereavement leave is time off work that a person can take after someone close has died.
exercise: «Many churches run bereavement support groups; people of all beliefs use counsellors and helplines.» What does bereavement mean? | *The loss of a close relative or friend because they have died | Pets that have been lost for a short time | A type of bird that lives near churches | A happy party for a new baby
exercise: The phrase «bereavement leave» means | *Time off work after someone close has died | Time off to watch a football match | Time off school for a holiday
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that means people who help others by listening. | groups | beliefs | churches | *counsellors
test: Mia's family had a bereavement last year. What does this mean? | They got a new puppy | They moved to a new house | They won a prize at the fair | *Someone close to them died
test: Which is the best example of a bereavement support group? | *A group where people who have lost someone meet and share their feelings | A football team for local kids | A group that sells cakes at the fair | A club where children learn chess
exam: Why might a writer choose the formal word bereavement instead of a plain word? | *It is a gentle, respectful way to talk about a death | It means a loud noise | It means a happy birthday | It is slang and means cool
